{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root-caused the six-change stack Verified -1 (epic f79d, mirror remediation).\n\nFinding 1 — the -1 votes are against STALE patchsets. Every pushed Gerrit revision differs from every local commit (gerrit 2530=11e669180ba1 2531=908d4f74d3dd 2533=436a687c102e 2535=ca5d08e6fa06 2536=bb76a00a8f55 2537=b7ed793101ab vs local 5a2819b14541 93fa6d1879b1 59b9f9fe8f74 c30c53992be6 f822f4ecb923 936178dad405). The stack was rebuilt locally and never pushed, so CI has never voted on the current code.\n\nFinding 2 — none of the failures was a test failure. Run 33688717373 (change 2537) failed the Public-types drift gate on all four platforms: that gate runs python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types and diffs src/rebar/types.py, a GENERATED file whose header says DO NOT EDIT BY HAND, and F3/F6/F7 all added constants to it. Runs 33687891644 and 33702178549 failed even earlier, in the Gerrit checkout step — git fetch origin misses the change ref on the GitHub mirror and the Gerrit fallback returned HTTP 504 after 60s, the disk-pressured host, i.e. the environmental class. Neither run contains a single FAILED tests/ line.\n\nFinding 3 — at the current local tip gen_types produces no diff; the generator now emits both TICKET_TYPES and PLAN_REVIEW_EXEMPT_TYPES, so the drift cause is addressed locally. Whether each INTERMEDIATE commit also passes is unproven and is what the next push will establish.\n\nMethod note, recorded because it nearly became a false root cause. I first checked the drift gate per-commit in a detached worktree using PYTHONPATH rather than a real editable install. It reported drift at every commit including the tip, contradicting the clean regeneration in the real worktree. The regenerated file had dropped ALL the enum Literals, meaning the generator could not resolve the schemas — an environment artifact, not evidence. Discarded rather than reported. A per-commit drift check needs a real install per commit.\n\nAlso this session: F8 (91b0) implemented and pushed as change 2548, now LLM-Review +1. F9 re-review PASS+signed after its unsatisfiable AC1b was corrected; change 2547 LLM-Review +1. bc66 plan corrected after a justified BLOCK (nothing imports Finding from _cli._registry; the real consumer surface is eight names across 22 files), re-review in flight. F10 plan written with its three drift claims re-verified, file_impact recorded BEFORE review, review in flight. F14 review in flight."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788400784818334001,"uuid":"b3f360a4-bc9f-44a2-a1f8-97c609c1e5cd"}